{"stamp": "1790847705377388449-3762437", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Functor/Basic.lean", "line_start": 130, "line_end": 130, "replacement": "-- Natural isomorphisms are also provided in `Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Functor/Category.lean`\n-- (`Functor.rightUnitor` and `Functor.leftUnitor`)."}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
{"stamp": "1790847710633814157-3762657", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Preserves/Over.lean", "line_start": 14, "line_end": 15, "replacement": "Note that `Over.forget X : Over X ⥤ C` already preserves all colimits when `C` has binary products,\nbecause it is then a left adjoint (`Over.forgetAdjStar`, see\n`Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Comma/Over/Pullback.lean`)."}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
{"stamp": "1790847719723600742-3762957", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Localization/Equivalence.lean", "line_start": 14, "line_end": 22, "replacement": "In `Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Localization/Predicate.lean`, the lemma\n`Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalence_target` already showed that the predicate of localized\ncategories is unchanged when we replace the target category (i.e. the candidate localized category)\nby an equivalent category.\nIn this file, we show the same for the source category\n(`Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalence_source`).\nMore generally, `Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalences` shows that we may replace both the\nsource and target categories by equivalent categories. This is obtained using\n`Localization.isEquivalence` which provides a sufficient condition in order to show\nthat a functor between localized categories is an equivalence."}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
{"stamp": "1790847724320266407-3763186", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Preserves/Limits.lean", "line_start": 13, "line_end": 16, "replacement": "If `G` preserves limits, and `C` and `D` have limits, then for any diagram `F : J ⥤ C` we have a\ncanonical isomorphism `preservesLimitIso : G.obj (limit F) ≅ limit (F ⋙ G)`.\nWe also show that we can commute `IsLimit.lift` of a preserved limit with `Functor.mapCone`:\n`(isLimitOfPreserves G t).lift (G.mapCone c₂) = G.map (t.lift c₂)` (`preserves_lift_mapCone`)."}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
